WEBVTT

00:00:00.251 --> 00:00:08.808
Chapter 7, in which Kanga and Baby Roo come to the forest, and Piglet has a bath.

00:00:08.868 --> 00:00:17.384
Nobody seemed to know where they came from, but there they were in the forest, Kanga and Baby Roo.

00:00:17.444 --> 00:00:35.518
When Poo asked Christopher Robin, how did they come here, Christopher Robin said, in the usual way, if you know what I mean, Poo, and Poo, who didn't, said, oh, Then he nodded his head twice and said, in the usual way, ah.

00:00:35.578 --> 00:00:42.750
Then he went a call upon his friend Piglet to see what he thought about it, and at Piglet's house he found Rabbit.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:45.890
So they all talked about it together.

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:49.161
What I don't like about it is this, said Rabbit.

00:00:49.221 --> 00:01:05.806
Here are we, you, Poo, and you, Piglet, and me and suddenly and eo, said poo, and eo, and then suddenly, and owl, said poo, and owl, and then all of a sudden, oh, and eo, said poo.

00:01:05.866 --> 00:01:07.762
I was forgetting him.

00:01:07.822 --> 00:01:17.004
Here we are,' said Rabbit, this slowly and carefully, all of us.

00:01:17.064 --> 00:01:21.086
And then suddenly we wake up one morning and what do we find?

00:01:21.146 --> 00:01:30.743
We find a strange animal among us, an animal of whom we had never even heard before, an animal who carries her family about with her in her pocket.

00:01:30.803 --> 00:01:36.977
Suppose I carried my family about with me in my pocket, how many pockets should I want?

00:01:37.037 --> 00:01:38.788
Sixteen!

00:01:38.848 --> 00:01:41.428
Seventeen, isn't it, Sir Rabbit?

00:01:41.488 --> 00:01:45.789
And one more for a handkerchief that's eighteen, eighteen pockets in one suit.

00:01:45.849 --> 00:01:47.920
I haven't time.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:51.431
There was a long and thoughtful silence.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:58.962
And then Poo, who'd been frowning very hard for some minutes, said, I make it fifteen.

00:01:59.022 --> 00:02:00.142
What?

00:02:00.202 --> 00:02:01.273
Sir Rabbit.

00:02:01.333 --> 00:02:02.703
Fifteen.

00:02:02.763 --> 00:02:03.733
Fifteen.

00:02:03.793 --> 00:02:04.584
What?

00:02:04.643 --> 00:02:06.174
Your family.

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:08.019
What about them?

00:02:08.078 --> 00:02:14.146
Poo rubbed his nose and said that he thought Rabbit had been talking about his family.

00:02:14.206 --> 00:02:15.586
Did I?

00:02:15.646 --> 00:02:17.217
Said Rabbit, carelessly.

00:02:17.277 --> 00:02:19.018
Yes, you said.

00:02:19.078 --> 00:02:20.408
Never mind Poo.

00:02:20.468 --> 00:02:21.949
Said Piglet impatiently.

00:02:22.009 --> 00:02:25.550
The question is, what are we going to do about Kanga?

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:27.482
Oh, I see.

00:02:27.542 --> 00:02:28.762
Said Poo.

00:02:28.822 --> 00:02:31.733
The best way, said Rabbit, would be this.

00:02:31.793 --> 00:02:35.534
The best way would be to steal Baby Roo and hide him.

00:02:35.594 --> 00:02:41.536
And then when Kanga says, where's Baby Roo, we say, aha!

00:02:41.596 --> 00:02:43.378
Aha!

00:02:43.438 --> 00:02:44.848
Said Pooh, practicing.

00:02:44.908 --> 00:02:46.459
Aha!

00:02:46.519 --> 00:02:48.240
Aha!

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.240
Of course, he went on.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:54.812
We could say, aha, even if we hadn't stolen Baby Roo.

00:02:54.872 --> 00:02:57.512
Pooh, said Rabbit kindly.

00:02:57.572 --> 00:02:59.572
You haven't any brain.

00:02:59.632 --> 00:03:02.364
I know," said Poo humbly.

00:03:02.424 --> 00:03:08.248
We say aha, so that Kanga knows that we know where Baby Roo is.

00:03:08.308 --> 00:03:14.384
Aha means we'll tell you where Baby Roo is if you promise to go away from the forest and never come back.

00:03:14.444 --> 00:03:16.751
Now, don't talk while I think.

00:03:16.811 --> 00:03:22.078
who went into a corner and tried saying aha in that sort of voice.

00:03:22.138 --> 00:03:28.219
Sometimes it seemed to him that it did mean what Rabbit said, and sometimes it seemed to him that it didn't.

00:03:28.279 --> 00:03:31.530
I suppose it's just practice, he thought.

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:37.421
I wonder if Kanga will have to practice too so as to understand it.

00:03:37.481 --> 00:03:42.538
There's just one thing, said Piglet, fidgeting a bit.

00:03:42.598 --> 00:03:51.361
I was talking to Christopher Robin and he said that a kanga was generally regarded as one of the fiercer animals.

00:03:51.421 --> 00:04:00.568
I'm not frightened of fiercer animals in the ordinary way but it is well known that a one of the fiercer animals is deprived of its young.

00:04:00.628 --> 00:04:11.566
It becomes as fiercer as two of the fiercer animals in which case aha is perhaps a foolish thing to say.

00:04:11.626 --> 00:04:16.279
said Rabbit, taking out a pencil and licking the end of it.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:17.831
You haven't any pluck."

00:04:17.851 --> 00:04:23.336
"'It is hard to be brave,' said Piglet, sniffing slightly.

00:04:23.356 --> 00:04:27.300
"'When you're only a very small animal?'"

00:04:27.359 --> 00:04:37.262
Rabbit, who had begun to write very busily, looked up and said, "'It is because you are a very small animal that you will be useful in the adventure before us.'

00:04:37.322 --> 00:04:43.267
Piglet was so excited at the idea of being useful that he forgot to be frightened anymore.

00:04:43.327 --> 00:04:52.020
And when Rabbit went on to say that kangas were only fierce during the winter months, being at other times of an affectionate disposition, he could hardly sit still.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:56.050
He was so eager to begin being useful at once.

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:59.221
What about me, said Poo, sadly?

00:04:59.281 --> 00:05:01.728
I suppose I shan't be useful.

00:05:01.787 --> 00:05:03.505
Never mind, poo!"

00:05:03.565 --> 00:05:05.108
said Piglet, comfortingly.

00:05:05.167 --> 00:05:07.270
Another time, perhaps.

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:14.741
Without poo, said Rabbit, solemnly as he sharpened his pencil, the adventure would be impossible.

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:15.852
Ah!

00:05:15.912 --> 00:05:19.434
said Piglet, and tried not to look disappointed.

00:05:19.494 --> 00:05:29.208
But Poo went into a corner of the room and said proudly to himself, impossible without me, that sort of bear.

00:05:29.268 --> 00:05:37.254
Now listen, all of you said Rabbit when he'd finished writing, and Poo and Piglet sat listening very eagerly with their mouths open.

00:05:37.314 --> 00:05:40.728
This was what Rabbit read out.

00:05:40.787 --> 00:05:44.646
Plan to capture baby rule.

00:05:44.706 --> 00:05:45.832
1.

00:05:45.892 --> 00:05:47.554
General remarks.

00:05:47.614 --> 00:05:51.357
Kanga runs faster than any of us, even me.

00:05:51.416 --> 00:05:52.417
2.

00:05:52.477 --> 00:05:54.429
More general remarks.

00:05:54.488 --> 00:06:00.582
Kanga never takes her eye off Baby Roo, except when he safely buttoned up in her pocket.

00:06:00.642 --> 00:06:01.674
3.

00:06:01.734 --> 00:06:10.820
Therefore, if we are to capture Baby Roo, we must get a long start, because Kanga runs faster than any of us, even me.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:12.200
See one.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:13.552
4.

00:06:13.612 --> 00:06:14.950
A thought.

00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:25.226
If Roo had jumped out of Kanga's pocket and Piglet had jumped in, Kanga wouldn't know the difference because Piglet is a very small animal.

00:06:25.286 --> 00:06:27.288
Five, like Roo.

00:06:27.348 --> 00:06:34.314
Six, but Kanga would have to be looking the other way first so as not to see Piglet jumping in.

00:06:34.374 --> 00:06:36.656
Seven, C2.

00:06:36.716 --> 00:06:39.348
eight, another thought.

00:06:39.408 --> 00:06:46.675
But if Pooh was talking to her very excitedly, she might look the other way for a moment.

00:06:46.735 --> 00:06:47.646
Nine.

00:06:47.706 --> 00:06:50.088
And then I could run away with Rue.

00:06:50.148 --> 00:06:50.949
Ten.

00:06:51.009 --> 00:06:51.980
Quickly.

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:52.950
Eleven.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:57.084
And Canger wouldn't discover the difference until afterwards.

00:06:57.144 --> 00:07:04.371
Well, Rabbit read this out proudly, and for a little while after he'd read it, nobody said anything.

00:07:04.430 --> 00:07:11.497
And then Piglet, who will be opening and shutting his mouth without making any noise, managed to say very huskily.

00:07:11.557 --> 00:07:16.582
And afterwards, how do you mean?

00:07:16.642 --> 00:07:23.208
When Kanga does discover the difference, then we all say, aha!

00:07:23.268 --> 00:07:25.030
All three of us?

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:27.201
Yes.

00:07:27.261 --> 00:07:30.254
Why, what's the trouble, Piglet?

00:07:30.314 --> 00:07:32.056
Nothing.

00:07:32.116 --> 00:07:34.979
As long as we all three say it.

00:07:35.039 --> 00:07:38.610
As long as we all three say it.

00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:40.872
I don't mind, he said.

00:07:40.932 --> 00:07:45.323
But I shouldn't care to say a harper myself.

00:07:45.383 --> 00:07:47.965
It wouldn't sound nearly so well.

00:07:48.024 --> 00:07:54.788
By the way, he said, you are quite sure about what you said about the winter months.

00:07:54.847 --> 00:07:56.682
The winter months?

00:07:56.742 --> 00:08:00.858
Yes, only being fierce in the winter months.

00:08:00.918 --> 00:08:03.048
Oh, yes, yes, that's all right.

00:08:03.108 --> 00:08:05.670
Well, Poo, you see what you have to do?

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:07.800
No, said Poo Bear.

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:09.551
Not yet, he said.

00:08:09.611 --> 00:08:11.082
What do I do?

00:08:11.142 --> 00:08:16.404
Well, you just have to talk very hard to Clanger so she doesn't notice anything.

00:08:16.464 --> 00:08:17.514
Oh.

00:08:17.574 --> 00:08:19.044
What about?

00:08:19.104 --> 00:08:20.770
Anything you like?

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:24.496
You mean, like, telling her a little bit of poetry or something?

00:08:24.556 --> 00:08:25.807
That's it, said Rabbit.

00:08:25.827 --> 00:08:26.588
Splendid!

00:08:26.648 --> 00:08:28.288
Now, come along.

00:08:28.348 --> 00:08:32.202
So, they all went out to look for Kanga.

00:08:32.261 --> 00:08:38.486
Kanga and Roo were spending a quiet afternoon in a sandy part of the forest.

00:08:38.546 --> 00:08:44.520
Baby Roo was practicing very small jumps in the sand and falling down mouse holes and climbing out of them.

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:49.844
And Kanga was fidgeting about and saying, just one more jump there and then you must go home.

00:08:49.904 --> 00:08:54.438
And, at that moment, who should come stumping up the hill but poo?

00:08:54.498 --> 00:08:57.030
Good afternoon, Kanga.

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:59.041
Good afternoon, poo.

00:08:59.101 --> 00:09:01.132
Look at me jumping!

00:09:01.152 --> 00:09:04.584
The squeak grew and fell into another mouse hole.

00:09:04.644 --> 00:09:07.306
Hello, Rue, my little fellow.

00:09:07.366 --> 00:09:09.968
We were just going home, said Kanga.

00:09:10.028 --> 00:09:11.229
Good afternoon, Rabbit.

00:09:11.289 --> 00:09:13.056
Good afternoon, Piglet.

00:09:13.116 --> 00:09:24.161
Rabbit and Piglet, who had now come up from the other side of the hill, said good afternoon, and hello, Rue, and Rue asked them to look at him jumping, so they stayed and looked.

00:09:24.222 --> 00:09:26.504
And Canger looked too.

00:09:26.564 --> 00:09:32.120
Oh, Canger, said Poo, after Rabbit had winked at him twice.

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:36.664
I don't know if you are interested in poetry at all.

00:09:36.724 --> 00:09:39.654
Hardly at all, said Canger.

00:09:39.714 --> 00:09:41.474
Oh, said Poo.

00:09:41.534 --> 00:09:45.737
Rudeer, just one more jump, and then we must go home.

00:09:45.797 --> 00:09:50.711
There was a short silence while Rue fell down another mousehole.

00:09:50.771 --> 00:09:55.024
Go on, said Rabbit, in a loud whisper behind his paw.

00:09:55.084 --> 00:10:02.430
And, talking of poetry, said Poo, I made up a little piece as I was coming along.

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:04.012
It went like this.

00:10:04.072 --> 00:10:05.493
Let me see.

00:10:05.553 --> 00:10:09.106
Fancy, said Now, rude, dear.

00:10:09.166 --> 00:10:12.018
You'll like this piece of poetry, said Rabbit.

00:10:12.078 --> 00:10:13.638
You love it.

00:10:13.698 --> 00:10:14.799
Said Piglet.

00:10:14.859 --> 00:10:17.210
You must listen very carefully, said Rabbit.

00:10:17.270 --> 00:10:19.712
So I's not to miss any of it.

00:10:19.772 --> 00:10:20.832
Said Piglet.

00:10:20.892 --> 00:10:21.883
Are you?

00:10:21.943 --> 00:10:23.064
Said Kanga.

00:10:23.124 --> 00:10:25.846
But she still looked at Baby Row.

00:10:25.906 --> 00:10:29.208
How did it go, a poo?

00:10:29.268 --> 00:10:30.708
Said Rabbit.

00:10:30.768 --> 00:10:34.642
Poo gave a little cough and began.

00:10:34.702 --> 00:10:40.098
Lines written by a bear of very little brain.

00:10:40.158 --> 00:10:45.092
On Monday when the sun is hot, I wonder to myself a lot.

00:10:45.152 --> 00:10:47.704
Now is it true or is it not?

00:10:47.764 --> 00:10:51.017
That what is which and which is what?

00:10:51.076 --> 00:10:56.931
On Tuesday when it hails and snows, the feeling on me grows and grows.

00:10:56.991 --> 00:11:02.778
That hardly anybody knows if those are these or these are those.

00:11:02.838 --> 00:11:13.912
On Wednesday, when the sky is blue and I have nothing else to do, I sometimes wonder if it's true that who is what and what is who.

00:11:13.972 --> 00:11:26.340
On Thursday, when it starts to freeze and whore-frost twinkles on the trees, how very readily one sees that these are whose, but whose are these?

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:28.159
on Friday.

00:11:28.219 --> 00:11:30.211
Yes, it is, isn't it?"

00:11:30.271 --> 00:11:33.003
said Canger, not waiting to hear what happened on Friday.

00:11:33.063 --> 00:11:36.796
Just one more jump road here, then we really must be going.

00:11:36.856 --> 00:11:40.450
Rabbit gave Pooh a hurrying up sort of nudge.

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:44.313
The talking of poetry, said Pooh quickly.

00:11:44.373 --> 00:11:48.838
Have you ever noticed that tree right over there?

00:11:48.898 --> 00:11:50.008
Where?

00:11:50.068 --> 00:11:51.159
said Canger.

00:11:51.179 --> 00:11:54.304
Now, Rue, right over there.

00:11:54.364 --> 00:11:57.168
said Pooh, pointing behind Kanga's back.

00:11:57.228 --> 00:11:59.009
"'No,' said Kanga.

00:11:59.069 --> 00:12:00.850
"'Now, jump in Rudy and we go home.

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:04.451
"'You ought to look at that tree right over there,' said Rabbit.

00:12:04.471 --> 00:12:05.912
"'Shall I lift you in, Rue?'

00:12:05.972 --> 00:12:08.123
And he picked up Rue in his paws.

00:12:08.183 --> 00:12:11.194
"'I can see a bird in it from here,' said Pooh.

00:12:11.214 --> 00:12:12.685
"'Or is it a fish?'

00:12:12.745 --> 00:12:14.755
"'You want to see that bird from here?'

00:12:14.815 --> 00:12:16.396
said Rabbit, unless it is a fish.

00:12:16.416 --> 00:12:19.856
"'It isn't a fish, it's a bird,' said Piglet.

00:12:19.876 --> 00:12:21.577
"'So it is,' said Rabbit.

00:12:21.597 --> 00:12:23.957
"'Is it a starling or a black bird?'

00:12:24.017 --> 00:12:24.537
said Pooh.

00:12:24.557 --> 00:12:26.688
"'That's the whole question,' said Rabbit.

00:12:26.748 --> 00:12:28.928
"'Is it a black bird or a starling?'

00:12:28.988 --> 00:12:34.019
And then at last, Kanga did turn her head to look.

00:12:34.079 --> 00:12:40.328
And the moment that her head was turned, Rabbit said, in a loud voice, In you go, Roo!

00:12:40.388 --> 00:12:48.742
and in jumped Piglet into Kanga's pocket, and off-scampered Rabbit with Roo in his paws as fast as he could.

00:12:48.802 --> 00:12:50.783
Why, where's Rabbit?

00:12:50.843 --> 00:12:52.764
said Kanga, turning round again.

00:12:52.824 --> 00:12:54.766
Are you all right, Roo dear?

00:12:54.826 --> 00:13:00.218
Piglet made a squeaky, Roo noise from the bottom of Kanga's pocket.

00:13:00.278 --> 00:13:03.850
Rabbit had to go away, said Pooh.

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:08.042
I think he thought of something he had to go and see about, suddenly.

00:13:08.102 --> 00:13:10.242
and piglet.

00:13:10.302 --> 00:13:14.576
I think piglet thought of something at the same time suddenly.

00:13:14.636 --> 00:13:17.439
Well, we must be getting home," said Kanga.

00:13:17.499 --> 00:13:18.980
Goodbye, Poo.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:23.654
And in three large jumps, she was gone.

00:13:23.714 --> 00:13:27.267
Poo looked after her as she went.

00:13:27.328 --> 00:13:30.800
I wish I could jump like that, he thought.

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:34.103
Some can and some can't.

00:13:34.164 --> 00:13:35.992
That's how it is.

00:13:36.052 --> 00:13:39.889
But there were moments when Piglet wished that Kanga couldn't.

00:13:39.949 --> 00:13:54.424
Often, when he'd had a long walk home through the forest, he'd wished that he were a bird, but now he thought jerkily to himself at the bottom of Kanga's pocket, if this is flying, I shall never really take to it.

00:13:54.484 --> 00:14:10.800
And as he went up in the air, he said, oh, and as he came down, he said, oh, and he was saying, oh, oh, oh, all the way to Kanger's house.

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:16.833
Of course, as soon as Kanger unbuttoned her pocket, she saw what had happened.

00:14:16.893 --> 00:14:19.754
Just for a moment, she thought she was frightened.

00:14:19.814 --> 00:14:26.398
And then she knew she wasn't, for she felt sure that Christopher Robin would never let any harm happen to Rue.

00:14:26.458 --> 00:14:34.349
So she said to herself, if they are having a joke with me, I will have a joke with them.

00:14:34.409 --> 00:14:38.828
Now then, rude here, she said, and she took Piglet out of her pocket.

00:14:38.888 --> 00:14:40.260
Bet time!

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:42.141
Aha!

00:14:42.201 --> 00:14:45.614
said Piglet, as well as he could after his terrifying journey.

00:14:45.674 --> 00:14:50.208
But it wasn't a very good aha, and Kanger didn't seem to understand what it meant.

00:14:50.268 --> 00:14:54.316
Bath first said Kanger in a cheerful voice.

00:14:54.376 --> 00:14:59.114
said Piglet again, looking round anxiously for the others, but the others weren't there.

00:14:59.174 --> 00:15:11.390
Rabbit was playing with Baby Roo in his own house and feeling more fond of him every minute, and Poo, who had decided to be a kanga, was still at the sandy place on the top of the forest, practicing jumps.

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:20.154
I'm not at all sure, said Kanga, in a thoughtful voice, that it wouldn't be a good idea to have a cold bath this evening.

00:15:20.214 --> 00:15:22.466
Would you like that rude ear?

00:15:22.526 --> 00:15:32.422
Piglet, who had never been really fond of baths, shuddered a long, indignant shudder, and said in as brave a voice as he could.

00:15:32.482 --> 00:15:34.254
Canger!

00:15:34.314 --> 00:15:38.656
I see that the time has come to speak plainly.

00:15:38.716 --> 00:15:43.548
Funny little Rue, said Canger, as she got the bath water ready.

00:15:43.608 --> 00:15:45.539
I am not Rue!

00:15:45.599 --> 00:15:47.801
said Piglet loudly.

00:15:47.861 --> 00:15:56.382
Yes, dear, yes, said Kanga soothingly, and imitating Piglet's voice too, so clever of him.

00:15:56.442 --> 00:16:00.336
She went on as she took a large bar of yellow soap out of the cupboard.

00:16:00.396 --> 00:16:02.498
What will he be doing next?

00:16:02.558 --> 00:16:04.001
Can't you see?

00:16:04.061 --> 00:16:06.524
Shouted Piglet, haven't you got any eyes?

00:16:06.584 --> 00:16:07.558
Look at me!

00:16:07.618 --> 00:16:10.891
I am looking rude dear," said Kanga, rather severely.

00:16:10.951 --> 00:16:13.842
And you know what I told you yesterday about making faces.

00:16:13.902 --> 00:16:20.894
If you go on making faces like piglets, you will grow up to look like piglet and then think how sorry you'll be.

00:16:20.954 --> 00:16:25.786
Now then, into the bath and don't let me have to speak to you about it again."

00:16:25.846 --> 00:16:35.344
Before he knew where he was, Piglet was in the bath, and Kanga was scrubbing him firmly with a large, lathery flannel.

00:16:35.404 --> 00:16:37.242
cried Piglet.

00:16:37.302 --> 00:16:39.284
Let me out on Piglet!

00:16:39.344 --> 00:16:42.596
Don't open the mouth, dear, or the soap goes in, said Canger.

00:16:42.656 --> 00:16:43.227
There!

00:16:43.287 --> 00:16:45.539
What did I tell you?

00:16:45.599 --> 00:16:48.701
You did it on purpose!

00:16:48.761 --> 00:16:54.986
Spluttered Piglet as soon as he could speak again, and then accidentally had another mouth full of lathery flannel.

00:16:55.046 --> 00:16:58.829
That's right, dear, don't say anything, said Canger.

00:16:58.890 --> 00:17:03.792
And in another minute Piglet was out of the bath and being rubbed dry with the towel.

00:17:03.852 --> 00:17:08.423
Now, said Kanga, there she met some and then bed.

00:17:08.484 --> 00:17:11.225
Well, what met some?

00:17:11.285 --> 00:17:12.326
Said Piglet.

00:17:12.386 --> 00:17:18.600
To make you grow big and strong dear, you don't want to grow up small and weak like Piglet, do you?

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:20.100
Well then.

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:22.912
At that moment there was a knock at the door.

00:17:22.973 --> 00:17:25.133
Come in, said Kanga.

00:17:25.194 --> 00:17:27.614
And in came Christopher Robin.

00:17:27.675 --> 00:17:30.105
Christopher Robin, Christopher Robin!

00:17:30.165 --> 00:17:35.586
cried Piglet, tell Kanga who I am, she keeps saying I'm Ru, I'm not Ru, am I?

00:17:35.646 --> 00:17:40.718
Christopher Robin looked at him very carefully and shook his head.

00:17:40.778 --> 00:17:47.981
You can't be Ru, he said, because I've just seen Ru playing in Rabbit's house.

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:52.132
Well, said Kanga, fancy that.

00:17:52.192 --> 00:17:55.392
Fancy my making a mistake like that.

00:17:55.452 --> 00:17:57.481
There you are, said Piglet.

00:17:57.542 --> 00:17:59.123
I told you so.

00:17:59.183 --> 00:18:00.904
I'm Piglet.

00:18:00.964 --> 00:18:03.746
Christopher Robin shook his head again.

00:18:03.807 --> 00:18:05.818
Oh, you're not Piglet.

00:18:05.878 --> 00:18:08.971
He said, I know Piglet well.

00:18:09.032 --> 00:18:11.969
And he's quite a different colour.

00:18:12.029 --> 00:18:31.790
Piglet began to say that this was because he had just had a bath, and then he thought that perhaps he wouldn't say that, and as he opened his mouth to say something else, Canger slipped the medicine spoon in, and then patted him on the back and told him that it was really quite a nice taste when you got used to it.

00:18:31.850 --> 00:18:34.903
I knew it wasn't Piglet, said Canger.

00:18:34.963 --> 00:18:37.778
I wonder who it can be.

00:18:37.838 --> 00:18:42.322
Perhaps it's some relation of poo's, said Christopher Robin.

00:18:42.382 --> 00:18:46.274
What about a nephew or an uncle or something?

00:18:46.335 --> 00:18:53.168
Kanga agreed that this was probably what it was and said that they would have to call it by some name.

00:18:53.228 --> 00:19:01.042
I shall call it Pookel, said Christopher Robin, Henry Pookel for short.

00:19:01.102 --> 00:19:06.654
And just when he was decided, Henry Poodle wriggled out of Kanga's arms and jumped to the ground.

00:19:06.714 --> 00:19:10.525
To his great joy, Christopher Robin had left the door open.

00:19:10.585 --> 00:19:20.137
Never had Henry Poodle piglet run so fast as he ran then, and he didn't stop running until he got quite close to his house.

00:19:20.198 --> 00:19:31.334
But when he was 100 yards away, he stopped running and rolled the rest of the way home, so as to get his own nice, comfortable colour again.

00:19:31.394 --> 00:19:36.032
So Kanga and Roo stayed in the forest.

00:19:36.092 --> 00:19:41.145
And every Tuesday Roo spent the day with his great friend, Rabbit.

00:19:41.206 --> 00:19:47.750
And every Tuesday Kanga spent the day with her great friend, Poo, teaching him to jump.

00:19:47.810 --> 00:19:54.266
And every Tuesday Piglet spent the day with his great friend, Christopher Robin.

00:19:54.326 --> 00:19:58.758
So they were all happy again.

00:19:58.818 --> 00:20:07.674
Chapter 8, in which Christopher Robin leads an expedition to the North Pole.

00:20:07.734 --> 00:20:12.948
One fine day, Poo had stumped up to the top of the forest.

00:20:13.008 --> 00:20:17.082
To see of his friend Christopher Robin was interested in bears at all.

00:20:17.142 --> 00:20:22.256
At breakfast that morning, a simple meal of marmalade spread lightly over a honeycomb or two.

00:20:22.316 --> 00:20:24.827
He had suddenly thought of a new song.

00:20:24.888 --> 00:20:27.144
It began like this.

00:20:27.204 --> 00:20:31.581
Sing, ho, for the light, for the bear.

00:20:31.641 --> 00:20:42.110
When you've got as far as this, he scratched his head and thought to himself, that's a very good start for a song, but what about the second line?

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:48.354
He tried singing, ho, two or three times, but it didn't seem to help.

00:20:48.414 --> 00:20:55.480
Perhaps it would be better, he thought, if I sang, hi, for the life of a bear.

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:57.383
So he sang it.

00:20:57.443 --> 00:20:59.446
but it wasn't.

00:20:59.506 --> 00:21:15.473
Very well then, he said, I shall sing that first line twice, and perhaps if I sing it very quickly, I shall find myself singing the third and fourth lines before I have time to think of them, and that will be a good song.

00:21:15.534 --> 00:21:21.466
Now then, Sing, oh, for the life of a bear.

00:21:21.526 --> 00:21:24.957
Sing, oh, for the life of a bear.

00:21:25.017 --> 00:21:31.088
I don't much mind if it rains or snows, because I've got a lot of honey on my nice new nose.

00:21:31.148 --> 00:21:37.600
I don't much care if it snows or thaws, because I've got a lot of honey on my nice clean paws.

00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:40.110
Sing, oh, for a bear.

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:48.772
Sing, oh, for a poo and I'll have a little something in an hour or two.

00:21:48.832 --> 00:21:54.635
He was so pleased with this song that he sang it all the way to the top of the forest.

00:21:54.695 --> 00:22:02.788
And if I go on singing it much longer, he thought, it will be time for the little something, and then the last line won't be true.

00:22:02.848 --> 00:22:07.190
So he turned it into a hum instead.

00:22:07.250 --> 00:22:12.238
Christopher Robin was sitting outside his door, putting on his big boots.

00:22:12.298 --> 00:22:18.017
As soon as he saw the big boots, Poo knew that an adventure was going to happen.

00:22:18.077 --> 00:22:26.612
And he brushed the honey off his nose with the back of his paw and spruced himself up as well as he could, so as to look ready for anything.

00:22:26.672 --> 00:22:30.014
Good morning, Christopher Robin, he called out.

00:22:30.074 --> 00:22:31.756
Hello, Poo Bear.

00:22:31.816 --> 00:22:33.816
I can't get this boot on.

00:22:33.876 --> 00:22:36.716
That's bad, said Poo.

00:22:36.776 --> 00:22:40.438
Do you think you could very kindly lean against me?

00:22:40.498 --> 00:22:44.170
Because I keep pulling so hard that I fall over backwards."

00:22:44.231 --> 00:22:51.036
Poo sat down, dug his feet into the ground and pushed hard against Christopher Robin's back.

00:22:51.096 --> 00:22:58.202
And Christopher Robin pushed hard against his and pulled and pulled his boot until he had got it on.

00:22:58.262 --> 00:23:00.984
And that's that, said Poo.

00:23:01.044 --> 00:23:02.856
What do we do next?

00:23:02.916 --> 00:23:08.481
We are all going on an expedition," said Christopher Robin, as he got up and brushed himself.

00:23:08.541 --> 00:23:09.452
Thank you, Poo.

00:23:09.472 --> 00:23:15.736
"'Going on an expedition,' said Poo eagerly, "'I don't think I've ever been on one of those.

00:23:15.756 --> 00:23:18.818
"'Where are we going to on this expedition?'"

00:23:18.878 --> 00:23:21.480
"'Expedition,' Sally Albert.

00:23:21.500 --> 00:23:22.941
"'It's got an X in it.'

00:23:22.961 --> 00:23:25.142
"'Oh,' said Poo.

00:23:25.162 --> 00:23:27.213
"'I know.'

00:23:27.274 --> 00:23:28.504
But he didn't really.

00:23:28.524 --> 00:23:32.574
"'We're going to discover the North Pole.

00:23:32.634 --> 00:23:35.190
Oh, said Pooh again.

00:23:35.250 --> 00:23:38.221
What is the North Pole, he asked?

00:23:38.281 --> 00:23:45.103
It's just a thing you discover, said Christopher Robin carelessly, not being quite sure himself.

00:23:45.163 --> 00:23:48.374
Oh, I see, said Pooh.

00:23:48.434 --> 00:23:52.354
Are bears any good at discovering it?

00:23:52.414 --> 00:23:53.945
Of course they are.

00:23:54.005 --> 00:23:57.666
And rabbit and kanga and all of you, it's an expedition.

00:23:57.726 --> 00:24:02.905
That's what an expedition means, a long line of everybody.

00:24:02.965 --> 00:24:06.646
You better tell the others to get ready while I see my guns all right.

00:24:06.706 --> 00:24:09.788
And we must all bring provisions.

00:24:09.848 --> 00:24:11.439
Bring what?

00:24:11.499 --> 00:24:13.270
Things to eat.

00:24:13.330 --> 00:24:16.183
Oh, said Poo happily.

00:24:16.242 --> 00:24:18.944
I thought you said provisions.

00:24:19.004 --> 00:24:20.596
I'll go and tell them.

00:24:20.656 --> 00:24:22.607
And he stumped off.

00:24:22.668 --> 00:24:25.720
The first person he met was Rabbit.

00:24:25.780 --> 00:24:27.811
Hello, Rabbit, he said.

00:24:27.871 --> 00:24:29.290
Is that you?

00:24:29.350 --> 00:24:32.889
Pretend it isn't," said Rabbit, and see what happens.

00:24:32.949 --> 00:24:34.800
I've got a message for you.

00:24:34.860 --> 00:24:36.270
I'll give it to him.

00:24:36.330 --> 00:24:41.042
We're all going on an expedition with Christopher Robin.

00:24:41.102 --> 00:24:43.173
What is it when we're on it?

00:24:43.233 --> 00:24:47.264
A sort of boat, I think, said Pooh.

00:24:47.284 --> 00:24:48.085
Oh, that's sort.

00:24:48.145 --> 00:24:51.666
Yes, and we're going to discover a pole or something.

00:24:51.686 --> 00:24:54.277
Or was it a mole?

00:24:54.337 --> 00:24:56.950
Anyhow, we're going to discover it.

00:24:57.010 --> 00:24:58.283
We are, are we?

00:24:58.343 --> 00:24:59.254
Said rabbit.

00:24:59.314 --> 00:25:06.026
Yes, and we've got to bring pro things to eat with us in case we want to eat them.

00:25:06.086 --> 00:25:08.137
Now I'm going down to piglets.

00:25:08.197 --> 00:25:10.132
Tell Kanga, will you?

00:25:10.192 --> 00:25:13.559
He left Rabbit and hurried down to Piglet's house.

00:25:13.619 --> 00:25:24.476
The Piglet was sitting on the ground at the door of his house, blowing happily at a dandelion and wondering whether it would be this year, next year, sometime or never.

00:25:24.536 --> 00:25:35.563
He had just discovered that it would be never and was trying to remember what it was and hoping it wasn't anything nice when Poo came up.

00:25:35.623 --> 00:25:38.645
Oh, Piglet, said Poo, excitedly.

00:25:38.705 --> 00:25:43.787
We're going on an expedition, all of us, with things to eat, to discover something.

00:25:43.847 --> 00:25:45.728
To discover what?

00:25:45.788 --> 00:25:47.829
Said Piglet, anxiously.

00:25:47.889 --> 00:25:50.610
Oh, just something?

00:25:50.671 --> 00:25:53.172
Nothing fierce.

00:25:53.232 --> 00:25:56.793
Christopher Robin didn't say anything about fierce.

00:25:56.853 --> 00:25:59.684
He just said it had an X.

00:25:59.744 --> 00:26:02.526
It isn't their next, her mind.

00:26:02.586 --> 00:26:04.218
said piglet earnestly.

00:26:04.279 --> 00:26:05.600
It said teeth!

00:26:05.660 --> 00:26:09.844
But if Christopher Robin is coming, I don't mind anything.

00:26:09.904 --> 00:26:16.494
In a little while they were all ready at the top of the forest and the expedition started.

00:26:16.554 --> 00:26:33.768
First came Christopher Robin and Rabbit, then Piglet and Pooh, then Canger with Rue in her pocket, and Owl, then Eor, and at the end in a long line all Rabbit's friends and relations.

00:26:33.828 --> 00:26:39.312
I didn't ask them, explain Rabbit carelessly, they just came, they always do.

00:26:39.372 --> 00:26:48.362
They can march at the end after Eor, What I say, said Eor, is that it's unsettling.

00:26:48.382 --> 00:26:55.464
I didn't want to come on this expo, what pool said.

00:26:55.524 --> 00:27:07.338
I only came to oblige, but here I am, and if I am the end of the expo, what we're talking about, then let me be the end.

00:27:07.398 --> 00:27:23.581
But if every time I want to sit down for a little rest, I have to brush away half a dozen of rabbits, smaller friends and relations first, then this isn't an expo, whatever it is at all.

00:27:23.641 --> 00:27:27.362
It's simply a confused noise.

00:27:27.422 --> 00:27:29.712
That's what I say.

00:27:29.772 --> 00:27:33.385
I see what Eeyore means, said Owl.

00:27:33.445 --> 00:27:39.418
If you ask me, I'm not asking anybody, said Eeyore.

00:27:39.478 --> 00:27:42.740
I'm just telling everybody.

00:27:42.800 --> 00:27:51.966
We can look for the North Pole, or we can play here we go gathering nuts and may, with the end part of an ant's nest.

00:27:52.026 --> 00:27:54.876
It's all the same to me.

00:27:54.936 --> 00:27:57.567
There was a shout from the top of the line.

00:27:57.587 --> 00:27:59.988
"'Come on,' called Christopher Robin.

00:28:00.008 --> 00:28:02.750
"'Come on,' called Pooh and Piglet.

00:28:02.770 --> 00:28:04.511
"'Come on,' called Owl.

00:28:04.531 --> 00:28:06.772
"'We're starting,' said Rabbit.

00:28:06.792 --> 00:28:07.903
"'I must go.'

00:28:07.963 --> 00:28:12.116
And he hurried after the front of the expedition with Christopher Robin.

00:28:12.176 --> 00:28:14.957
"'All right,' said Eor.

00:28:14.977 --> 00:28:16.738
"'We're going.

00:28:16.758 --> 00:28:20.020
"'Only don't blame me.'

00:28:20.040 --> 00:28:25.098
"'So off they all went to discover the pole.

00:28:25.158 --> 00:28:32.856
And, as they walked, they chatted to each other of this and that, all except Poo, who was making up a song.

00:28:32.916 --> 00:28:37.670
This is the first verse he said to Piglet when he was ready with it.

00:28:37.730 --> 00:28:39.670
First verse of what?

00:28:39.731 --> 00:28:41.062
My song.

00:28:41.122 --> 00:28:42.482
What song?

00:28:42.542 --> 00:28:43.553
This one.

00:28:43.613 --> 00:28:44.854
Which one?

00:28:44.914 --> 00:28:48.116
Well, if you listen, Piglet, you'll hear it.

00:28:48.176 --> 00:28:51.048
How do you know I'm not listening?

00:28:51.108 --> 00:28:53.709
Poo couldn't answer that one.

00:28:53.769 --> 00:28:55.976
So he began to sing.

00:28:56.037 --> 00:29:02.515
They all went off to discover the pole, Owl and Piglet and Rabbit and all.

00:29:02.575 --> 00:29:08.398
It's a thing you discover as I've been told by Owl and Piglet and Rabbit and all.

00:29:08.458 --> 00:29:14.710
You're Christopher Robin and Pooh and Rabbit's relations all went through.

00:29:14.770 --> 00:29:24.180
And where the pole was none of them knew, Sing hey for Owl and Rabbit and all.

00:29:24.240 --> 00:29:27.819
said Christopher Robin, turning round to Pooh.

00:29:27.879 --> 00:29:31.251
We are just coming to a dangerous place.

00:29:31.311 --> 00:29:35.654
Hush said Pooh, turning round quickly to Piglet.

00:29:35.714 --> 00:29:38.416
Hush said Piglet to Canger.

00:29:38.476 --> 00:29:45.070
Hush said Canger to Owl, while Rue said Hush several times to himself, but he quietly.

00:29:45.130 --> 00:29:48.478
Hush said Owl to Eel.

00:29:48.538 --> 00:29:51.077
Hush!"

00:29:51.137 --> 00:30:01.488
said Eo in a terrible voice to all rabbit friends and relations, and hush they said hastily to each other all down the line, until it got to the last one of all.

00:30:01.548 --> 00:30:10.016
And the last and smallest friend in relation was so upset to find that the whole expedition was saying hush to him.

00:30:10.077 --> 00:30:21.746
that he buried himself head downwards in a crack in the ground and stayed there for two days until the danger was over and then went home in a great hurry and lived quietly with his aunt ever afterwards.

00:30:21.806 --> 00:30:26.200
His name was Alexander Beatle.

00:30:26.260 --> 00:30:36.385
They had come to a stream which twisted and tumbled between high rocky banks and Christopher Roberts saw at once how dangerous it was.

00:30:36.445 --> 00:30:40.938
It's just the place, he explained, for an ambush.

00:30:40.998 --> 00:30:44.041
What sort of bush was put poo to piglet?

00:30:44.101 --> 00:30:45.693
A gorse bush?

00:30:45.753 --> 00:30:52.370
My dear poo, said Al in his superior way, don't you know what an ambush is?

00:30:52.430 --> 00:30:56.253
Al, said piglet, looking round at him severely.

00:30:56.313 --> 00:31:01.973
Poof Whisper was a perfectly private whisper, and there was no need.

00:31:02.033 --> 00:31:07.105
An ambush, said Owl, is a sort of surprise.

00:31:07.165 --> 00:31:10.876
So is the gorse bush, sometimes, said Pooh.

00:31:10.936 --> 00:31:18.309
An ambush, as I was about to explain to Pooh, said Piglet, is a sort of surprise.

00:31:18.369 --> 00:31:23.497
If people jump out at you suddenly, that's an ambush, said Owl.

00:31:23.557 --> 00:31:27.854
It's an ambush, Pooh, when people jump at you suddenly!"

00:31:27.914 --> 00:31:29.614
explained Piglet.

00:31:29.674 --> 00:31:41.256
Pooh, who now knew what an ambush was, said that a gorse-busch had sprung at him suddenly one day when he fell off a tree, and he had taken six days to get all the prickles out of himself.

00:31:41.317 --> 00:31:47.128
We are not talking about gorse-bushes, said Owl, a little crossly.

00:31:47.188 --> 00:31:49.702
I am, said Pooh.

00:31:49.762 --> 00:31:55.222
They were climbing very cautiously up the stream now, going from rock to rock.

00:31:55.282 --> 00:32:06.624
And after they'd gone a little way, they came to a place where the banks widened out at each side, so that on each side of the water, there was a level strip of grass on which they could sit down and rest.

00:32:06.684 --> 00:32:11.258
As soon as he saw this, Christopher Robin called, halt!

00:32:11.318 --> 00:32:14.529
And they all sat down and rested.

00:32:14.588 --> 00:32:23.024
I think, said Christopher Robin, that we ought to eat all our provisions now, so that we shan't have so much to carry.

00:32:23.084 --> 00:32:24.835
Eat all our what?

00:32:24.895 --> 00:32:25.896
said Pooh.

00:32:25.956 --> 00:32:27.347
Oh, that we've brought!

00:32:27.407 --> 00:32:29.208
said Piglet, getting to work.

00:32:29.268 --> 00:32:31.890
That's a good idea, said Pooh.

00:32:31.950 --> 00:32:34.082
And he got to work too.

00:32:34.142 --> 00:32:36.394
Have you all got something?

00:32:36.454 --> 00:32:38.676
asked Christopher Robin with his mouth full.

00:32:38.736 --> 00:32:41.178
All except me.

00:32:41.238 --> 00:32:42.349
Said Eor.

00:32:42.409 --> 00:32:44.551
As usual.

00:32:44.611 --> 00:32:48.784
He looked round at them in his melancholy way.

00:32:48.844 --> 00:32:54.636
I suppose none of you were sitting on a thistle by an enchant.

00:32:54.696 --> 00:32:57.808
I believe I am, said Pooh.

00:32:57.868 --> 00:32:59.028
Ow!

00:32:59.088 --> 00:33:01.049
He got up and looked behind him.

00:33:01.109 --> 00:33:03.160
Yes, I was.

00:33:03.220 --> 00:33:04.900
I thought so.

00:33:04.961 --> 00:33:07.222
Thank you, Pooh.

00:33:07.282 --> 00:33:10.784
If you've quite finished with it.

00:33:10.844 --> 00:33:15.172
He moved across to Pooh's place and began to eat.

00:33:15.232 --> 00:33:25.322
It doesn't do them any good, you know, sitting on them," he went on, as he looked up, munching, takes all the life out of them.

00:33:25.382 --> 00:33:29.303
Remember that another time, all of you.

00:33:29.323 --> 00:33:37.078
A little consideration, a little thought for others makes all the difference.

00:33:37.138 --> 00:33:43.652
As soon as he had finished his lunch, Christopher Robin whispered to Rabbit, and Rabbit said, yes, yes, of course.

00:33:43.712 --> 00:33:46.733
And they walked a little way up the stream together.

00:33:46.793 --> 00:33:50.244
I didn't want the others to hear, said Christopher Robin.

00:33:50.304 --> 00:33:53.515
Quite so, said Rabbit, looking important.

00:33:53.575 --> 00:34:00.456
It's, I wonder, it's only, Rabbit, I suppose you don't know.

00:34:00.516 --> 00:34:03.716
What does the North Pole look like?

00:34:03.776 --> 00:34:09.580
Well, said Rabbit, stroking his whiskers, now you're asking me.

00:34:09.640 --> 00:34:14.515
I did know once only I've sort of forgotten, said Christopher Robin carelessly.

00:34:14.575 --> 00:34:23.963
It's a funny thing, said Rabbit, but I've sort of forgotten too, although I did know once I suppose it's just a pole stuck in the ground.

00:34:24.023 --> 00:34:33.624
Sure to be a pole, said Rabbit, because of calling it a pole, and if it's a pole, well I should think it would be sticking in the ground, shouldn't you, because there'd be nowhere else to stick it.

00:34:33.685 --> 00:34:35.882
Yes, that's what I thought.

00:34:35.942 --> 00:34:41.111
The only thing, said Rabbit, is where is it sticking?

00:34:41.171 --> 00:34:44.664
That's what we're looking for, said Christopher Robin.

00:34:44.725 --> 00:34:46.833
They went back to the others.

00:34:46.894 --> 00:34:49.977
Piglet was lying on his back, sleeping peacefully.

00:34:50.037 --> 00:35:00.006
Ru was washing his face and paws in the stream, while Kanga explained to everybody proudly that this was the first time he had ever washed his face himself.

00:35:00.066 --> 00:35:10.066
And all was telling Kanga an interesting anecdote full of long words like encyclopedia and rhododendron to which Kanga wasn't listening.

00:35:10.127 --> 00:35:14.642
I don't all with all is washing grumbled eaw.

00:35:14.702 --> 00:35:18.114
This modern behind the ears nonsense.

00:35:18.174 --> 00:35:21.096
What do you think, Pooh?"

00:35:21.156 --> 00:35:28.952
Well, said Pooh, I think, but we shall never know what Pooh thought.

00:35:29.012 --> 00:35:35.990
For they came a sudden squeak from Rue, a splash, and a loud cry of alarm from Canger.

00:35:36.050 --> 00:35:40.454
So much for washing, said Eeyore.

00:35:40.514 --> 00:35:46.418
Roo's fallen in, cried Rabbit, and he and Christopher Robin came rushing down to the rescue.

00:35:46.478 --> 00:35:49.009
Look at me swimming!

00:35:49.069 --> 00:35:54.622
Sweet Roo from the middle of his pool, and was hurried down a waterfall into the next pool.

00:35:54.682 --> 00:35:56.533
Are you all right, Roo dear?

00:35:56.593 --> 00:35:58.114
called Canger, anxiously.

00:35:58.174 --> 00:35:59.955
Yes, said Roo.

00:36:00.015 --> 00:36:01.846
Look at me, sweet!

00:36:01.906 --> 00:36:06.194
And down he went over the next waterfall into another pool.

00:36:06.254 --> 00:36:08.983
Everybody was doing something to help.

00:36:09.043 --> 00:36:14.868
Piglet, wide awake suddenly, was jumping up and down and making, Oh, I say, noises.

00:36:14.928 --> 00:36:22.266
Owl was explaining that in a case of sudden and temporary immersion, the important thing was to keep the head above water.

00:36:22.326 --> 00:36:26.960
Canger was jumping along the bank saying, Are you sure you're all right, Rudia?

00:36:27.020 --> 00:36:32.768
To which room, from whatever pool he was in at the moment, was answering, little bees, swimming!

00:36:32.828 --> 00:36:49.576
Eeyore had turned round and hung his tail over the first pool into which Rue fell, and with his back to the accident was grumbling quietly to himself and saying, Oh, this washing, but catch on to my tail, little Rue, and you'll be alright.

00:36:49.636 --> 00:36:55.088
And Christopher Robin and Rabbit came hurrying past Eeyore and were calling out to the others in front of them.

00:36:55.148 --> 00:36:57.959
All right, Rue, I'm coming, call Christopher Robin.

00:36:58.019 --> 00:37:01.941
Get something across the stream lower down, some of you fellas, called Rabbit.

00:37:02.001 --> 00:37:05.433
But Poo was getting something.

00:37:05.493 --> 00:37:17.328
Two pools below Roo, he was standing with a long pole in his paws, and Kanga came up and took one end of it, and between them they held it across the lower part of the pool.

00:37:17.388 --> 00:37:22.138
And Roo, still bubbling proudly, look at me, swimming!

00:37:22.198 --> 00:37:25.320
drifted up against it and climbed out.

00:37:25.380 --> 00:37:26.951
Did you see me swimming?

00:37:27.011 --> 00:37:30.544
Squeaked through, excitedly, while Kanga scolded him and rubbed him down.

00:37:30.604 --> 00:37:32.125
Pooh, did you see me swimming?

00:37:32.185 --> 00:37:34.527
That's called swimming, what I was doing?

00:37:34.587 --> 00:37:36.199
Rabbit, did you see what I was doing?

00:37:36.259 --> 00:37:39.902
Swimming, I got piglet, I got piglet, what did you think I was doing?

00:37:39.962 --> 00:37:41.653
Swimming!

00:37:41.713 --> 00:37:44.086
Gritte of a Robin, did you see me?

00:37:44.146 --> 00:37:46.708
But Christopher Robin wasn't listening.

00:37:46.768 --> 00:37:48.870
He was looking at Pooh.

00:37:48.930 --> 00:37:51.359
Pooh, he said.

00:37:51.419 --> 00:37:54.038
Where did you find that pole?

00:37:54.098 --> 00:37:57.420
Poo looked at the pole in his hands.

00:37:57.480 --> 00:38:00.042
I just found it, he said.

00:38:00.102 --> 00:38:01.873
I thought it ought to be useful.

00:38:01.913 --> 00:38:03.564
I just picked it up.

00:38:03.624 --> 00:38:07.266
Poo said Christopher Robin solemnly.

00:38:07.326 --> 00:38:10.468
The expedition is over.

00:38:10.529 --> 00:38:15.091
You have found the North Pole.

00:38:15.151 --> 00:38:18.704
Oh, said Poo.

00:38:18.764 --> 00:38:23.388
Eeyore was sitting with his tail in the water when they all got back to him.

00:38:23.448 --> 00:38:27.459
Tell Rue to be quick, somebody, he said.

00:38:27.519 --> 00:38:30.010
My tail's getting cold.

00:38:30.030 --> 00:38:33.872
I don't want to mention it, but I just mention it.

00:38:33.932 --> 00:38:36.813
I don't want to complain, but there it is.

00:38:36.873 --> 00:38:39.734
My tail's cold.

00:38:39.794 --> 00:38:42.565
Here I am, sweet Rue.

00:38:42.625 --> 00:38:45.136
Oh, there you are.

00:38:45.156 --> 00:38:47.890
Did you see me swimming?

00:38:47.950 --> 00:38:53.458
Eeyore took his tail out of the water and swished it from side to side.

00:38:53.518 --> 00:39:03.848
As I expected, he said, lost all feeling, numbed it, that's what it's done, numbed it.

00:39:03.908 --> 00:39:08.668
Well, as long as nobody minds, I suppose it's all right.

00:39:08.728 --> 00:39:13.355
poor oldie, or I'll dry it for you," said Christopher Robin.

00:39:13.415 --> 00:39:15.816
And he took out his handkerchief and rubbed it up.

00:39:15.877 --> 00:39:18.588
Thank you, Christopher Robin.

00:39:18.648 --> 00:39:23.272
You're the only one who seems to understand about tales.

00:39:23.332 --> 00:39:28.165
They don't think that's what's the matter with some of these others.

00:39:28.225 --> 00:39:30.507
They've no imagination.

00:39:30.527 --> 00:39:33.929
A tale isn't a tale to them.

00:39:33.989 --> 00:39:38.244
It's just a little bit extra at the back.

00:39:38.304 --> 00:39:42.058
Never mind, Eor, said Christopher Robin, rubbing his hardest.

00:39:42.118 --> 00:39:43.598
Is that better?

00:39:43.658 --> 00:39:47.732
It's feeling more like a tale, perhaps.

00:39:47.792 --> 00:39:51.565
It belongs again, if you know what I mean.

00:39:51.585 --> 00:39:56.118
Hello, Eor, said Poo, coming up to them with his pole.

00:39:56.178 --> 00:39:58.060
Hello, Poo.

00:39:58.120 --> 00:40:04.055
Thank you for asking, but I shall be able to use it again in a day or two.

00:40:04.115 --> 00:40:06.576
Use what, said Poo.

00:40:06.636 --> 00:40:09.506
What we're talking about.

00:40:09.566 --> 00:40:13.587
I wasn't talking about anything, said Pooh, looking puzzled.

00:40:13.647 --> 00:40:23.479
My mistake again, I thought you were saying, how sorry you were about my tail being all numb, and could you do anything to help?

00:40:23.539 --> 00:40:25.610
No, said Pooh.

00:40:25.670 --> 00:40:28.060
That wasn't me, he said.

00:40:28.120 --> 00:40:32.072
He thought for a little, and then suggested, hopefully.

00:40:32.132 --> 00:40:34.540
Perhaps it was somebody else.

00:40:34.600 --> 00:40:39.681
Well, thank him for me when you see him.

00:40:39.742 --> 00:40:43.534
Poo looked anxiously at Christopher Robin.

00:40:43.594 --> 00:40:46.816
Poo's found the North Pole, said Christopher Robin.

00:40:46.876 --> 00:40:48.288
Isn't that lovely?

00:40:48.348 --> 00:40:51.130
Poo looked modestly down.

00:40:51.190 --> 00:40:53.021
Is that it?

00:40:53.081 --> 00:40:54.182
Said Eor.

00:40:54.242 --> 00:40:56.123
Yes, said Christopher Robin.

00:40:56.183 --> 00:40:59.246
Is that what we were looking for?

00:40:59.306 --> 00:41:01.938
Yes, said Poo.

00:41:01.998 --> 00:41:05.469
Oh, said Eor.

00:41:05.529 --> 00:41:11.601
Well, anyhow, it didn't rain, he said.

00:41:11.662 --> 00:41:16.164
They stuck the pole in the ground and Christopher Robin tied a message onto it.

00:41:16.225 --> 00:41:20.776
North Pole, discovered by Poo.

00:41:20.837 --> 00:41:23.668
Poo found it.

00:41:23.728 --> 00:41:25.980
Then they all went home again.

00:41:26.040 --> 00:41:32.615
And I think, but I'm not quite sure, that Rue had a hot bath and went straight to bed.

00:41:32.675 --> 00:41:45.452
But Poo went back to his own house and feeling very proud of what he had done, had a little something to revive himself.

00:41:45.512 --> 00:41:56.328
Chapter 9 In which Piglet is entirely surrounded by water.

00:41:56.388 --> 00:42:02.824
It rained, and it rained, and it rained.

00:42:02.884 --> 00:42:17.648
Piglet told himself that never, in all his life, and he was goodness knows how old, three was it, or four, never had he seen so much rain, days and days and days.

00:42:17.708 --> 00:42:33.876
If only he thought, as he looked out of the window, I had been in Pooh's House or Christopher Robin's House or Rabbit's House when it began to rain, then I should have had company all this time instead of being here, all alone with nothing to do except wonder when it will stop.

00:42:33.936 --> 00:42:38.939
And he imagined himself with Pooh saying, Did you ever see such rain, Pooh?

00:42:38.999 --> 00:42:41.360
And Pooh saying, Isn't it awful, Piglet?

00:42:41.420 --> 00:42:45.032
And Piglet saying, I wonder how it is of a Christopher Robin's way?

00:42:45.092 --> 00:42:49.556
And Pooh saying, I should think poor old Rabbit is about flooded out by this time.

00:42:49.616 --> 00:42:58.404
It would have been jolly to talk like this and really it wasn't much good having anything exciting like floods if you couldn't share them with somebody.

00:42:58.464 --> 00:43:00.884
For it was rather exciting.

00:43:00.944 --> 00:43:06.456
The little dry ditches in which Piglet had nosed about so often had become streams.

00:43:06.516 --> 00:43:23.666
The little streams across which he had splashed were rivers, and the river between whose steep banks they had played so happily had sprawled out of its own bed and was taking up so much room everywhere that Piglet was beginning to wonder whether it would be coming into his bed soon.

00:43:23.726 --> 00:43:31.732
It's a little anxious, he said to himself, to be a very small animal entirely surrounded by water.

00:43:31.792 --> 00:43:51.535
Christopher Robin and Poo could escape by climbing trees and kanga could escape by jumping and rabbit could escape by burrowing and how could escape by flying and you or could escape by making a loud noise until rescued and here am I surrounded by water and I can't do anything.

00:43:51.595 --> 00:44:02.436
It went on raining, and every day the water got a little higher until now it was nearly up to Piglet's window, and still he hadn't done anything.

00:44:02.496 --> 00:44:05.657
There's Pooh, he thought to himself.

00:44:05.717 --> 00:44:09.648
Pooh hasn't much brain, but he never comes to any harm.

00:44:09.708 --> 00:44:13.289
He does silly things and they turn out right.

00:44:13.349 --> 00:44:14.910
There's Howl.

00:44:14.970 --> 00:44:19.141
Howl hasn't exactly got brain, but he knows things.

00:44:19.201 --> 00:44:22.747
He would know the right thing to do when surrounded by water.

00:44:22.807 --> 00:44:29.174
There's rabbit, he hasn't learnt in books, but he can always think of a clever plan.

00:44:29.234 --> 00:44:39.167
There's kanga, she isn't clever, kanga isn't, but she would be so anxious about Ru that she would do a good thing to do without thinking about it.

00:44:39.227 --> 00:44:49.401
And then there's eel, and eel is so miserable anyhow that he wouldn't mind about this, but I wonder what Christopher Robin would do.

00:44:49.461 --> 00:45:01.571
Then suddenly he remembered a story which Christopher Robin had told him about a man on a desert island who had written something in a bottle and thrown it into the sea.

00:45:01.631 --> 00:45:09.337
And Piglet thought that if he wrote something in a bottle and threw it in the water, perhaps somebody would come and rescue him.

00:45:09.398 --> 00:45:19.132
He left the window and began to search his house, all of it that wasn't under water, and at last he found a pencil and a small piece of dry paper and a bottle with a cork to it.

00:45:19.192 --> 00:45:22.590
and he wrote on one side of the paper, Help!

00:45:22.650 --> 00:45:23.630
Piglet!

00:45:23.690 --> 00:45:24.671
Me!

00:45:24.731 --> 00:45:27.792
And on the other side, it's me, Piglet!

00:45:27.852 --> 00:45:28.293
Help!

00:45:28.353 --> 00:45:29.143
Help!

00:45:29.203 --> 00:45:41.961
Then he put the paper in the bottle and he corked the bottle up as tightly as he could, and he lent out of his window as far as he could lean without falling in, and he threw the bottle as far as he could throw.

00:45:42.021 --> 00:45:53.336
And in a little while it bobbed up again on the water, and he watched it floating slowly away in the distance, until his eyes ached with looking.

00:45:53.396 --> 00:45:59.688
And sometimes he thought it was the bottle, and sometimes he thought it was just a ripple on the water which he was following.

00:45:59.748 --> 00:46:09.821
And then suddenly he knew that he would never see it again, and that he had done all that he could do to save himself.

00:46:09.881 --> 00:46:39.606
So now he thought somebody else will have to do something and I hope they'll do it soon because if they don't I shall have to swim which I can't so I hope they'll do it soon and then he gave a very long sigh and said I was poo here he's so much more friendly with two When the rain began, Pooh was asleep.

00:46:39.666 --> 00:46:44.148
It rained, and it rained, and it rained.

00:46:44.208 --> 00:46:48.810
And he slept, and he slept, and he slept.

00:46:48.870 --> 00:46:52.111
He had had a tiring day.

00:46:52.171 --> 00:46:55.012
You remember how he discovered the North Pole?

00:46:55.072 --> 00:47:03.846
Well, he was so proud of this that he asked Christopher Robin if there were any other poles such as a bear of little brain might discover.

00:47:03.906 --> 00:47:12.828
There's a South Pole," said Christopher Robin, and I expect there's an East Pole and a West Pole, though people don't like talking about them.

00:47:12.888 --> 00:47:20.291
Pooh was very excited when he heard this and suggested that they should have an expedition to discover the East Pole.

00:47:20.351 --> 00:47:28.514
But Christopher Robin had thought of something else to do with Kanga, so Pooh went out to discover the East Pole by himself.

00:47:28.574 --> 00:47:45.084
Whether he discovered it or not, I forget, but he was so tired when he got home that in the very middle of his supper, after he'd been eating for a little more than half an hour, he fell fast asleep in his chair, and slept, and slept, and slept.

00:47:45.144 --> 00:47:48.685
Then, suddenly, he was dreaming.

00:47:48.746 --> 00:47:57.587
He was at the East Pole, and it was a very cold pole, with the coldest sort of snow and ice all over it.

00:47:57.647 --> 00:48:06.286
He had found a beehive to sleep in, but there wasn't room for his legs, so he'd left them outside.

00:48:06.346 --> 00:48:14.107
And wild woozels, such as inhabit the East Pole, came and nibbled all the fur of his legs to make nests for their young.

00:48:14.167 --> 00:48:20.778
And the more they nibbled, the colder his legs got, until suddenly he woke up with them, aah!

00:48:20.838 --> 00:48:26.380
And there he was, sitting in his chair with his feet in the water.

00:48:26.440 --> 00:48:29.322
and water all round him.

00:48:29.382 --> 00:48:32.443
He splashed to his door and looked out.

00:48:32.503 --> 00:48:35.284
This is serious, said Pooh.

00:48:35.344 --> 00:48:37.624
I must have an escape.

00:48:37.685 --> 00:48:48.092
So he took his largest pot of honey and escaped with it to a broad branch of his tree, well above the water, and then he climbed down again and escaped with another pot.

00:48:48.152 --> 00:48:57.094
And when the whole escape was finished, there was Poo sitting on his branch dangling his legs, and there beside him were ten pots of honey.

00:48:57.154 --> 00:49:05.830
Two days later, there was Poo sitting on his branch dangling his legs, and there beside him were four pots of honey.

00:49:05.890 --> 00:49:14.736
Three days later, there was Poo sitting on his branch dangling his legs, and there beside him was one pot of honey.

00:49:14.796 --> 00:49:18.702
Four days later, there was Poo.

00:49:18.762 --> 00:49:28.972
And it was on the morning of the fourth day that Piglet's bottle came floating past him, and with one loud cry of, Honey!

00:49:29.033 --> 00:49:34.848
Poo plunged into the water, seized the bottle, and struggled back to history again.

00:49:34.908 --> 00:49:40.512
Bother, said Poo as he opened it, all that wet for nothing.

00:49:40.572 --> 00:49:43.305
What's that bit of paper doing?

00:49:43.365 --> 00:49:45.960
He took it out and looked.

00:49:46.020 --> 00:49:49.036
It's a message, he said to himself.

00:49:49.096 --> 00:50:04.176
That's what it is, and that letter is a P, and so is that, and so is that, and P means poo, so it's a very important message to me, and I can't read it.

00:50:04.236 --> 00:50:14.296
I must find Christopher Robin or Owl or Piglet, one of those clever readers who can read things, and they will tell me what this message means.

00:50:14.357 --> 00:50:16.548
Only I can't swim.

00:50:16.608 --> 00:50:18.290
Bother.

00:50:18.350 --> 00:50:20.694
Then he had an idea.

00:50:20.754 --> 00:50:25.528
And I think that for a bear of very little brain, it was a good idea.

00:50:25.589 --> 00:50:38.276
He said to himself, If a bottle can float, then a jar can float, and if a jar floats, I can sit on the top of it, if it's a very big jar.

00:50:38.337 --> 00:50:42.948
So he took his biggest jar and caught it up.

00:50:43.008 --> 00:50:46.349
All boats have to have a name, he said.

00:50:46.409 --> 00:50:50.950
So I shall call mine the floating bear.

00:50:51.010 --> 00:50:56.149
And with these words, he dropped his boat into the water and jumped in after it.

00:50:56.208 --> 00:51:04.040
For a little while, poo and the floating bear were uncertain as to which of them was meant to be on the top.

00:51:04.100 --> 00:51:15.608
But after trying one or two different positions, they settled down with the floating bear underneath and poo triumphantly astrighted, paddling vigorously with his feet.

00:51:15.668 --> 00:51:20.232
Christopher Robin lived at the very top of the forest.

00:51:20.292 --> 00:51:23.758
It rained and it rained.

00:51:23.818 --> 00:51:27.764
but the water couldn't come up to his house.

00:51:27.824 --> 00:51:37.949
It was rather jolly to look down into the valleys and see the water all around him, but it rained so hard that he stayed indoors most of the time and thought about things.

00:51:38.009 --> 00:51:47.683
Every morning he went out with his umbrella and put a stick in the place where the water came up to, and every next morning he went out and couldn't see his stick anymore.

00:51:47.743 --> 00:51:51.196
So he put another stick in the place where the water came up to.

00:51:51.256 --> 00:51:59.641
And then he walked home again, and each morning he had a shorter way to walk than he had had the morning before.

00:51:59.701 --> 00:52:05.780
On the morning of the fifth day he saw the water all around him.

00:52:05.841 --> 00:52:13.350
and knew that for the first time in his life he was on a real island, which was very exciting.

00:52:13.410 --> 00:52:20.794
It was on this morning that Owl came flying over the water to say, How do you do to his friend Christopher Robin?

00:52:20.854 --> 00:52:24.446
I say Owl, say Christopher Robin, isn't this fun?

00:52:24.506 --> 00:52:25.946
I'm on an island!

00:52:26.006 --> 00:52:32.065
The atmospheric conditions had been very unfavourable lately, said Owl.

00:52:32.126 --> 00:52:33.341
The what?

00:52:33.401 --> 00:52:35.292
It has been raining!"

00:52:35.352 --> 00:52:36.692
explained Owl.

00:52:36.752 --> 00:52:38.833
Yes, said Christopher Robin.

00:52:38.893 --> 00:52:40.093
It has.

00:52:40.153 --> 00:52:44.804
The flood level has reached an unprecedented height.

00:52:44.864 --> 00:52:46.155
The who?

00:52:46.215 --> 00:52:49.076
There's a lot of water about, explained Owl.

00:52:49.136 --> 00:52:51.086
Yes, said Christopher Robin.

00:52:51.146 --> 00:52:51.956
There is.

00:52:52.016 --> 00:52:56.298
However, the prospects are rapidly becoming more favourable.

00:52:56.358 --> 00:52:59.759
At any moment, have you seen Poo?

00:52:59.819 --> 00:53:00.959
No.

00:53:01.019 --> 00:53:04.931
At any moment, I hope he's all right, said Christopher Robin.

00:53:04.991 --> 00:53:06.182
I've been wondering about him.

00:53:06.242 --> 00:53:07.842
I expect piglets with him.

00:53:07.902 --> 00:53:09.934
Do you think they're all right, Owl?

00:53:09.994 --> 00:53:11.864
I expect so.

00:53:11.924 --> 00:53:15.396
You see, at any moment, do go and see, Owl.

00:53:15.456 --> 00:53:18.958
Because Poo hasn't got very much brain and he might do something silly.

00:53:19.018 --> 00:53:20.709
And I do love him so, Owl.

00:53:20.769 --> 00:53:22.239
Do you see, Owl?

00:53:22.300 --> 00:53:24.621
That's all right, said, Owl.

00:53:24.681 --> 00:53:27.772
I'll go back directly.

00:53:27.832 --> 00:53:29.490
And he flew off.

00:53:29.550 --> 00:53:32.048
In a little while, he was back again.

00:53:32.108 --> 00:53:35.490
Pooh isn't there, he said.

00:53:35.550 --> 00:53:37.081
Not there.

00:53:37.141 --> 00:53:38.972
He's been there.

00:53:39.032 --> 00:53:44.485
He's been sitting on a branch of his tree outside his house with nine pots of honey.

00:53:44.545 --> 00:53:47.086
But he isn't there now.

00:53:47.146 --> 00:53:49.758
Pooh, cried Christopher Robin.

00:53:49.798 --> 00:53:51.038
Where are you?

00:53:51.098 --> 00:53:55.652
Here I am, said a growly voice behind him.

00:53:55.712 --> 00:53:57.666
Pooh!

00:53:57.726 --> 00:54:01.030
They rushed into each other's arms.

00:54:01.091 --> 00:54:03.391
How did you get here, Poo?

00:54:03.451 --> 00:54:07.002
asked Christopher Robin when he was ready to talk again.

00:54:07.062 --> 00:54:10.752
On my boat, said Poo proudly.

